Photoshop 26.10.0's own Duotone PSDs from the #1 Duotone phase 1b smokes
(scripts/photoshop-probe/duotone_take.py; the take itself moved to Duotone
phase 2, RULING-1 (b) 3). Each is the 104 x 24 scene (an 8-bit RGB TIFF of
R = G = B patches and a ramp) converted by Image > Mode > Grayscale (CnvM
Grys, Dot Gain 20%) and then Image > Mode > Duotone through one action
descriptor (CnvM T = duotoneMode), saved by a save descriptor (Pht3,
maximize compatibility, a copy).

duotone2-blank.psd: smoke1, attempt 1 (`inks`): two inks, "Warm Black" Lab
(20, 2, 4) and "Rust" Lab (55, 45, 55), Photoshop's default curves (0 % and
100 % set, the rest blank) and every overprint record blank. Copied from
~/devel/doctored-fixtures/photoshop/duotone-mode-547/smoke1/jobs/two/attempt-1.psd
(sha256 737b544a4b298166f1cff976def4c2df927f4af07d1d81e6ae830899cb305bb6).

duotone2-overprint.psd: smoke2, attempt 4 (`overprints`): the same inks and
curves with the 1+2 overprint given as Lab (6.19, 14.69, 9.21), the default
product W (.) P1/W (.) P2/W to 0.01. Copied from
~/devel/doctored-fixtures/photoshop/duotone-mode-547/smoke2/jobs/two/attempt-4.psd
(sha256 9580bc25c3857ec3d971fc9322d40de9f651702e4f6f7a621f2250a9b3750bc0).

Both hold colour-mode data of 524 bytes and the resources 1014 and 1017 (no
1018, no 1063). core/tests/duotone_files.rs reads them.

duotone3-curves.psd: the #1 Duotone phase 2b take (take1, case `three`).
Rasterize wrote the 104 x 24 scene (an untagged 8-bit gray PNG of the same
codes, opened under Dot Gain 20%) as a Tritone PSD through
core/examples/duotone_take_psd.rs: "Warm Black" Lab (20, 2, 4) curve 0 -> 100,
"Rust" Lab (55, 45, 55) curve 0 -> 10, 50 -> 30, 100 -> 70, "Lime" Lab
(80, -25, 70) curve 0 -> 0, 100 -> 50, every overprint the default. Photoshop
opened it (app.open) and saved it by a save descriptor (Pht3, maximize
compatibility, a copy); this is that save. Its colour-mode data (524 bytes:
the three inks and curves above, the four overprint records Lab, the rest
blank) is byte-equal to Rasterize's; its resources include 1014 and 1017 and
no ICC (1039). Copied from
~/devel/doctored-fixtures/photoshop/duotone-mode-547/take1/jobs/three/duotone3.psd
(sha256 68c77c9f5f4c47af695f492645e7363626b3e8f047149f25003ea806c9430477).
